<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Tagore returns two weeks after an indwelling catheter drained 680 mL from his bladder and tamsulosin 0.4 mg at bedtime was started. He feels better: the urgency and the four trips a night have gone, he sleeps through, and his appetite is returning. He has had no fever, pain, blood in the urine, or leakage. He empties the leg bag himself and his helpers manage the night bag; he washes around the catheter daily. He has had no dizziness on standing and no falls. Polyethylene glycol keeps his bowels regular. He had the kidney and bladder ultrasound this morning and saw Dr. Marsh-Okoro of urology afterwards. He continues his herbal preparation and will bring it to the next visit for the pharmacist. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Sleeping through; urgency gone</td></tr><tr><td>Catheter</td><td>Draining well; no fever, pain, blood, or leakage</td></tr><tr><td>Tamsulosin</td><td>No dizziness or falls</td></tr><tr><td>Bowels</td><td>Regular with polyethylene glycol</td></tr><tr><td>Ultrasound</td><td>This morning; reviewed today</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

